{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/952572-comparing-compacts-and-conspiracys-to-their-cwod-counterparts","id":952572,"title":"Comparing Compacts and Conspiracys to their CWOD Counterparts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-17T09:43:34-07:00","id":952572,"title":"Comparing Compacts and Conspiracys to their CWOD Counterparts","content":"How do the Malfeus Maleficium (sorry for the horrendous misspelling Cant be bothered to look it up) Compare to the society of leopold.<br /> <br /> or Task force Valkyrie to the SAD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:01:14-07:00","id":952579,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's much overlap between hunter organizations in cWoD and those in Vigil, apart from Malleus Maleficarum and the Society of Leopold. And I guess there's some sort of generic scholarly organization that could be an equivalent for Loyalists of Thule - but it doesn't have the legacy of supporting the Nazis that the Loyalists do. Besides, Vigil is based around the idea that was anathema to cWoD, namely that mortals can actually get something done now and again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:13:10-07:00","id":952590,"title":"","content":"If I'd make a comparison between Task Force VALKYRIE and a counterpart group in the WoD, I'd honestly go for the Technocracy. It's obviously not a one-for-one comparison, clearly; there are many facets to the Technocracy not reflected in VALKYRIE. The dehumanization, the cynical Machiavellian spirit of Control, the supergovernmental conspirators above any responsibility to others or any lack of resources. But for the contingent of folks who liked the angle of rank-and-file Technocratic field agents who believed in the greater good but went to extremes and compromised themselves to maintain it, I see a similar spirit at work with hoo-rah VALKYRIE special ops teams, busting out the Advanced Armory and playing fast and loose with due process to keep the free world working. Jackboots on the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T14:58:58-07:00","id":952759,"title":"","content":"What kind of comparison are you looking for specifically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T16:07:44-07:00","id":952813,"title":"","content":"The closest analog to the SAD is VASCU, actually. VASCU is basically just the SAD without the &quot;underfunded, near cancellation&quot; angle and a lot borrowed from Millennium. The Society of Leopold and the Malleus Maleficarum are close analogs.<br /> <br /> The Arcanum parallel the Loyalists pretty well except for their historical origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T18:22:34-07:00","id":952904,"title":"","content":"Division Six is the foot soldiers of the Technocracy, except they have no authority or tools and they're also wrong about everything.<br /> <br /> I love them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T18:40:47-07:00","id":952909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/952572-comparing-compacts-and-conspiracys-to-their-cwod-counterparts?p=952904#post952904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Division Six is the foot soldiers of the Technocracy, except they have no authority or tools and they're also wrong about everything.<br /> <br /> I love them!</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything he just said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:45:22-07:00","id":953281,"title":"","content":"Task Force Valkyrie has always seemed to me like what would happen if you brought all the CWoD government hunter groups (Project Twilight, the NSA guys with the &quot;Chaoscopes&quot;, etc.) and brought them all under one umbrella, along with some slightly Technocratic equipment upgrades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T00:06:03-07:00","id":953698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/952572-comparing-compacts-and-conspiracys-to-their-cwod-counterparts?p=952904#post952904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Division Six is the foot soldiers of the Technocracy, except they have no authority or tools and they're also wrong about everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends how 'realistic' you want to play it. If no one knows who you are, your legitimate authority isn't worth much. The cops will arrest you same as anyone else until your paperwork gets done properly.<br /> <br /> D6 don't have those issues, and the man in Panopticon may well be a better chocie for getting stuff done than sending a request up the TFV hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Actually, that's very like the Technocracy. It was always kinda implied that the black suits just used magic rather than having legitimate authority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T10:41:08-07:00","id":953908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/952572-comparing-compacts-and-conspiracys-to-their-cwod-counterparts?p=953698#post953698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends how 'realistic' you want to play it. If no one knows who you are, your legitimate authority isn't worth much. The cops will arrest you same as anyone else until your paperwork gets done properly.<br /> <br /> D6 don't have those issues, and the man in Panopticon may well be a better chocie for getting stuff done than sending a request up the TFV hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Actually, that's very like the Technocracy. It was always kinda implied that the black suits just used magic rather than having legitimate authority.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main difference there between TFV and D6 is that the TFV agents still exist within law enforcement bureaucracy and have credentials that can be verified pretty easily (even if what they really do is still classified). D6 doesn't have that, so if they get arrested they are SOL in short order. That being said, my assumption has always been that D6 agents are told &quot;We're so secret that no one knows who we are, so you can't trust local law enforcement. Everything you do is sanctioned by the government though, so don't be afraid to break the rules.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T11:01:54-07:00","id":953916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/952572-comparing-compacts-and-conspiracys-to-their-cwod-counterparts?p=953908#post953908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main difference there between TFV and D6 is that the TFV agents still exist within law enforcement bureaucracy and have credentials that can be verified pretty easily (even if what they really do is still classified). D6 doesn't have that, so if they get arrested they are SOL in short order. That being said, my assumption has always been that D6 agents are told &amp;quot;We're so secret that no one knows who we are, so you can't trust local law enforcement. Everything you do is sanctioned by the government though, so don't be afraid to break the rules.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The reason I love Division Six is because they're just budget Delta Green, and that's a fun niche to play in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T13:57:37-07:00","id":954022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/952572-comparing-compacts-and-conspiracys-to-their-cwod-counterparts?p=953916#post953916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. The reason I love Division Six is because they're just budget Delta Green, and that's a fun niche to play in.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I love them as NPCs, and briefly played one as a PC, I've never been able to center a an actual game around them from the perspective of PCs. I think the meta-knowledge that D6 is a sham makes them a little difficult for players to get into, in addition to the fact that their write-up doesn't make them out to be particularly sympathetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T14:24:40-07:00","id":954041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/952572-comparing-compacts-and-conspiracys-to-their-cwod-counterparts?p=954022#post954022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I love them as NPCs, and briefly played one as a PC, I've never been able to center a an actual game around them from the perspective of PCs. I think the meta-knowledge that D6 is a sham makes them a little difficult for players to get into, in addition to the fact that their write-up doesn't make them out to be particularly sympathetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>No more than 'cowboy' Delta Green is, though they have the benefit of not being played as dupes and having that hideous art that Division Six has. <br /> <br /> They're one of my favorite Compacts, right alongside Habibti Ma and Utopia Now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:17:58-07:00","id":954268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/952572-comparing-compacts-and-conspiracys-to-their-cwod-counterparts?p=953908#post953908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main difference there between TFV and D6 is that the TFV agents still exist within law enforcement bureaucracy and have credentials that can be verified pretty easily (even if what they really do is still classified).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know what the difference is, my point is that I don't think it'd help that much. 'Pretty easily' is still a night in a police holding cell; and if you're fighting a monster that's a really big problem. I mean, you can't exactly put your agents names on the national criminal databases because thousands of people have access to those.<br /> <br /> Also, again, D6 have Panopticon overseeing them. The guy may not care for the agents individually, but having them arrested is a problem as it reveals his lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:45:51-07:00","id":955103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/952572-comparing-compacts-and-conspiracys-to-their-cwod-counterparts?p=954268#post954268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I know what the difference is, my point is that I don't think it'd help that much. 'Pretty easily' is still a night in a police holding cell; and if you're fighting a monster that's a really big problem. I mean, you can't exactly put your agents names on the national criminal databases because thousands of people have access to those.<br /> <br /> Also, again, D6 have Panopticon overseeing them. The guy may not care for the agents individually, but having them arrested is a problem as it reveals his lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Verifying federal law enforcement credentials takes no more than five minutes (I checked with both local and federal law enforcement personnel). Unless they're doing something really blatantly shady and can't cover their asses they won't even be detained. This is assuming that they haven't already co-opted local enforcement to work with them. <br /> <br /> The best way for Panopticon to maintain its lie is to make sure its agents don't get arrested in the first place, even if it means killing cops. Whether or not it'll intervene when its agents get burned depends entirely on how important they are. If they're high ranking then sure, Panopticon has its own resources magical and otherwise to get them off the hook, but foot soldiers are easier to replace than rescue. Especially if it can convince their pinched agents that they have to &quot;go undercover&quot; for a while, and can spin the narrative that they've been &quot;flipped&quot; if for some reason they realized the truth and start trying to tell other agents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}